# s a_mend (p, v): a new array, s with its major cells at positions p
# replaced by v's cells in order, or by v alone when it is one cell; s
# itself is unchanged; a position given twice takes its last value; the
# axis subscript amends along another axis (A8, A6).
== SOURCE
s := 10 20 30 40
s a_mend (2 4, 0 9)
s a_mend (3, 7)
s a_mend (1 3, 5)
s
s a_mend (2 2, 1 2)
(2 3 r_eshape r_ange 6) a_mend (2, 0 0 0)
(2 3 r_eshape r_ange 6) a_mend_2 (1 3, 2 2 r_eshape 7 8 9 0)
"abc" a_mend (2, "X")
== RESULT
10 0 30 9
10 20 7 40
5 20 5 40
10 20 30 40
10 2 30 40
1 2 3
0 0 0
7 2 9
8 5 0
aXc
